>  From a pragmatic point of view, in Distance you could simply fit a
> detection function to the data from island B, and then get the
> probability of detection (P) and the corresponding standard error (se)
> from the Distance analysis. Then you run an analysis of the data of
> Island A only, force Distance to use a Uniform detection function with
> no adjustments, and then add a multiplier that is the P with the
> corresponding se. In this way, distance will do all the correct
> calculations for you and the reported results will be the same as if you
> had used the data from B to get the detection probability and the data
> from A for the encounter rate, which I believe is what you want (Is the
> maximum detection distance in both islands about the same?).
